---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="Food in MBR City"
  description="Dining and groceries across MBR City's communities — Meydan One's retail anchor, Riviera's promenade, and where the rest of the district actually eats."
>
  <section class="container hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Food</p>
    <h1>Where the district actually eats</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      One real anchor, one walkable exception, and everyone else driving
      to one or the other — that's the honest shape of dining across MBR
      City's communities.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Meydan One Mall</h2>
    <p>
      The district's main retail and dining anchor — cinema, restaurants,
      and a large-format mall experience most individual communities don't
      have on their own. District One and Sobha Hartland residents
      typically drive here or to Downtown/Business Bay for anything beyond
      community-level convenience retail.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Riviera's promenade</h2>
    <p>
      The exception: Riviera's ground-floor promenade covers a meaningful
      amount of day-to-day dining and grocery shopping without leaving the
      development. See <a href="https://riviera.dst.llc/food/">Riviera's own
      food page</a> for what's actually there.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>Groceries district-wide</h2>
    <p>
      Larger supermarkets cluster in Meydan and Business Bay; most
      individual communities have convenience-level grocery retail at best,
      Riviera's on-site supermarket being the closest thing to an
      exception.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

